cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the indexing result or the agent playbook, cite this repository. If you use the tables or the law list, cite the upstream projects as well."
title: "etp-residual-closure: closing 264 residual implications with already-published tables, and a playbook for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  264 implications that the Equational Theories Project proves finitely refutable
  but that carlok/parsimagma's construction corpus does not reach are all closed
  using ETP's own published Generated/All4x4Tables directory. 31 tables suffice;
  one 9-element table separates 137 of the 264. 206 of the 264 are separated by
  tables whose own Facts annotation never mentions them, which locates the defect
  in the index rather than in the search. Includes the reverse-index tool, three
  independent evaluators, per-pair witnesses with refuting assignments, and an
  operating manual for AI agents doing comparable corpus-alignment work.
type: software
license: MIT
